      "body": "Every new backend starts the same way for me. Instead of improvising, I keep a small template so I can get to real work faster.\n\n## Folder layout\n\nI split by responsibility, not by type:\n\n- `src/routes` for HTTP\n- `src/services` for business logic\n- `src/db` for data access\n\n## A strict tsconfig\n\nStrict mode catches a surprising number of bugs before they run:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"module\": \"NodeNext\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Express in a few lines\n\n```ts\nimport express from \"express\";\n\nconst app = express();\napp.use(express.json());\napp.get(\"/health\", (_req, res) => res.json({ ok: true }));\napp.listen(3000);\n```\n\nThat is the whole starting point. Everything else grows from here.",
