      "summary": "Where a cache actually helps, how I key it, and the invalidation rules that keep stale data from creeping in.",
      "body": "A cache is easy to add and easy to get wrong. Here is the checklist I run through.\n\n### 1. Cache reads, not truth\n\nThe database stays the source of truth. Redis only holds a fast copy.\n\n### 2. Key it clearly\n\n```\nuser:123:profile\n```\n\nNamespaced keys make it obvious what to delete later.\n\n### 3. Always set a TTL\n\n> A cache without expiry is just a second database you forgot to update.\n\nStart with a short TTL and lengthen it only when you have numbers to justify it.",
